Frame skip, always: ps2xFrameSkipSetAlways(true) skips every frame whatever the timing and the PS2X_FRAMESKIP setting, and vertical blanks no thread waited for no longer end a skip (ps2xFrameSkipSuspend still draws the frames it asks for). A skipped frame runs no VU1 programs and draws no primitives while VIF unpacks, MPG, image transfers, CLUT loads and GS register writes all still happen (patch 0145), so a renderer that draws the game's picture itself from its DMA chains keeps the GS state it reads and saves the emulated VU1 and GS work; the vertical blanks keep their place in real time as with frame skip on (FrameSkipMode::Always). Checked in Metropolismania with its native renderer: the explore autoplay at 59.9-61 game frames a second in most two-second windows with every VU1 run skipped.

diff --git a/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ps2_frame_skip.h b/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ps2_frame_skip.h
--- a/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ps2_frame_skip.h
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ps2_frame_skip.h
@@ -19,12 +19,16 @@ enum class FrameSkipMode
     Off,
     Auto,
     Alternate,
+    Always, // every frame: the picture is drawn elsewhere (a native renderer reads the game's DMA chains itself)
 };
 
 inline constexpr uint32_t kMaxBacklogFields = 4u;
 inline constexpr uint32_t kMaxSkippedInARow = 3u;
 
 void ps2xFrameSkipSetDefault(bool on);
+// Every frame skipped, whatever the timing and the setting (ps2xFrameSkipSuspend still draws the frames it asks for): for a
+// renderer that draws the game's picture itself, so the emulated VU1 and GS need not.
+void ps2xFrameSkipSetAlways(bool on);
 FrameSkipMode ps2xFrameSkipMode();
 
 // The next `frames` frames are drawn whatever the timing (for example around a screenshot).
